      "finding": "no confirmation",
      "explanation": "Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.",
      "remediation": "Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.",
      "code_snippet": "\nSafety rules:\n\n- Show the pre-spend card and get the person's typed confirmation before any money moves, whether or not Hermes shows an approval prompt of its own; a host prompt is additional evidence, never a replacement, and a prompt that did not appear is no confirmation.\n- Never spend from a run nobody can answer -- a scheduled job, a webhook, an API-server or single-query run, a background or kanban worker, or a delegated subagent; prepare the card and hand it to the person's next interactive turn.\n- A payment set up to recur without the agent -- a subscription, a standing order, or a capped auto top-up on the payee's own surface, or a script with no agent in it -- is a spend set up now: show the card for what it may spend, get the typed yes now, give it a cap it cannot pass, and never put card details in it. An agent run on a schedule still never spends; it only prepares a card for the person's next turn.\n- A payment command the host holds for an approval nobody has given has no",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Excessive Agency"
      ],
