      "finding": "no confirmation",
      "explanation": "Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.",
      "remediation": "Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.",
      "code_snippet": "owser_navigate`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_click`): read the quote and the receipt with them. A snapshot of the confirmation page with its order number is an observed receipt; a snapshot of the cart is a quote.\n- The approval prompt Hermes shows for a flagged command: when the paying command raises it, record its answer beside the typed confirmation. An auto-approval (`/yolo`, `approvals.mode: off`, or a call the default `smart` mode judged low-risk and approved itself) or a command the check did not flag is no confirmation at all.\n- The optional Hermes skills `stripe-link-cli` and `mpp-agent`, only when the person installed them. `stripe-link-cli` with `--request-approval` asks the person in their Link app, which is additional evidence beside the typed confirmation. `mpp-agent`'s `mppx` call pays the 402 as it runs and asks no one, so running it is the spend and comes only after the typed confirmation. The receipt either one returns fills `spend_receipt/v1`.\n\n## 3. Unknown outcomes",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Excessive Agency"
      ],
